// Tests that Vale does not lint content inside QDoc code blocks.
// Prose outside code blocks SHOULD warn; content inside SHOULD NOT.

// SHOULD WARN: passive voice in prose around \code block

/*!
    \fn void QFile::open()
    \brief Opens the file for reading and writing.

    The file is opened by calling this function.

    Call this function before reading any data:

    \code
    QFile file("example.txt");
    // We recommend utilizing this pattern in order to open files
    if (file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly)) {
        QByteArray data = file.readAll();
    }
    \endcode

    The data is returned as a QByteArray on \macos and \MACRO1.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: passive voice in prose around \qml block

/*!
    \qmltype FileDialog
    \brief Provides a dialog for selecting files.

    The dialog is shown by calling open():

    \qml
    FileDialog {
        // We recommend utilizing this pattern in order to show dialogs
        title: "Please choose a file"
        onAccepted: {
            console.log("You chose: " + fileDialog.selectedFile)
        }
    }
    \endqml

    The selected file is returned via the selectedFile property.
*/

// SHOULD WARN: wordiness in prose around \badcode block

/*!
    \fn void QTimer::start()
    \brief Starts the timer.

    Prior to calling start(), set the interval in milliseconds.
    Utilize stop() in order to cancel the timer.

    The following code is incorrect and should not be used:

    \badcode
    // We recommend utilizing this pattern in order to start timers
    QTimer timer;
    timer.start(-1);
    \endcode
*/
